{
  "name": "loss_logsigmoid_consensus_margin_cost",
  "intuition": "All parents converge on a stable pairwise preference objective: minimize a soft ranking loss via -logsigmoid of the log-probability difference (winner minus loser), with clamp for numerical stability and optional per-example weighting. A robust consensus improvement is to add a small non-negative margin so the model must not only prefer the winner but do so by at least a fixed amount, while keeping the optional detached cost gap shaping seen in some parents. This preserves the well-behaved, saturating gradient of logsigmoid, avoids exploding gradients via clamping, and uses detached cost information only as a bias term (not leaking gradients).",
  "theoretical_basis": "Pairwise logistic (Bradley-Terry) preference learning / DPO-style objective with a fixed margin and optional detached cost shaping; clamping stabilizes extreme logits.",
  "pseudocode": "d = lpw - lpl; x = alpha*scale*(d - margin) - cost_coef*detach(cost_b - cost_a); loss = -logsigmoid(clamp(x, -20, 20)); return mean(weight*loss)",
  "hyperparams": {
    "scale": 1.25,
    "margin": 0.05,
    "cost_coef": 0.1,
    "clamp_min": -20.0,
    "clamp_max": 20.0
  },
  "operators_used": [
    "logsigmoid",
    "clamp"
  ],
  "implementation_hint": {
    "expects": "batch['log_prob_w'], batch['log_prob_l'] required; batch.get('weight') optional; batch.get('cost_a'), batch.get('cost_b') optional; extra may contain 'alpha' and/or 'hyperparams' dict with keys scale, margin, cost_coef, clamp_min, clamp_max"
  },
  "code": "def generated_loss(batch, model_output, extra):\n    lpw = batch['log_prob_w']\n    lpl = batch['log_prob_l']\n    weight = batch.get('weight', None)\n\n    hp = extra.get('hyperparams', {}) if isinstance(extra, dict) else {}\n    alpha = float((extra.get('alpha', 1.0) if isinstance(extra, dict) else 1.0))\n    scale = float(hp.get('scale', 1.25))\n    margin = float(hp.get('margin', 0.05))\n    cost_coef = float(hp.get('cost_coef', 0.1))\n    clamp_min = float(hp.get('clamp_min', -20.0))\n    clamp_max = float(hp.get('clamp_max', 20.0))\n\n    d = lpw - lpl\n    x = alpha * scale * (d - margin)\n\n    if ('cost_a' in batch) and ('cost_b' in batch):\n        gap = (batch['cost_b'] - batch['cost_a']).detach()\n        x = x - cost_coef * gap\n\n    x = ops.clamp(x, clamp_min, clamp_max)\n    loss = -ops.logsigmoid(x)\n\n    if weight is not None:\n        loss = loss * weight\n\n    return loss.mean()",
